1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,043
The Compact votes to send a ring of soldiers. The stated reason is care. No second flood, no second tunnel, no second night of wet children. The guns are described as a fence.

2
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:14,468
Rim becomes a circle of white light pointed down. The lights are bright enough to read by, and too cold to sit under. The camp stops looking like a place where laundry would dry.

3
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:14,894
Dorje and the apprentices close the upper stair with masonry, and the roots of the garden terrace finish the work. It is a door grown shut. It is not a weapon. It does not chase.

4
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:11,489
The lamps are carried down, and the people follow the lamps. A city, Asha says, is the place where the lights go. The upper steps gather dust.

5
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:12,766
Dorje dies in his sleep, old, with the trowel on the peg where he always hung it. The apprentice takes it down in the morning and does not rename it.

6
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:13,617
Asha sweeps as far as the roots will allow. Beyond them she can hear boots, very faintly, and the chord, exactly on time. She talks to the stair as she always has.

7
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:15,319
Paper will fit where a person will not. Letters move through a thumb-wide gap. Some are from Jun to the camp. Some are from the camp to Jun. Reza sends one line: the latch was mine.

8
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:10,213
The long table is taken downstairs in pieces and rebuilt. The empty chair comes with it. Supper is later than usual, and it happens.

9
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:14,894
Vale stands at the lip and does not order the roots cut. He also does not send the army home. He says, to Imani, that he can no longer tell which choice is the restraint.

10
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:16,170
The decade closes with the ring intact and the lower rooms bright. The chord is muffled by living stone. It is not late. No one below has raised a hand. No one above has put the guns away.
